{"title":"What should I ask Paul Gillingham?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/944509523/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Paul-Gillingham.html","date":1770129674000,"content":"<p>Yes, I will be doing a Conversation with him.  He is a <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://history.northwestern.edu/people/faculty/core-faculty/paul-gillingham.html\" target=\"_blank\">Professor of History at Northwestern</a>, specializing in Mexico and to some extent the Caribbean.  He has translated <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Poe-Trauma-%C3%93scar-Xavier-Altamirano/dp/1787073327/ref=sr_1_1?crid=3HMEACTWFMZLT&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.m9Yt_WzZZgs2wGnSI30A1aox4JeL4qdYpokXMydXh2U.mG_4VmdO5hym-8nnqLccBl38emItFs4OWtRCjRpSZAI&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=Poe%3A+The+Trauma+of+an+Era&amp;qid=1770129139&amp;sprefix=poe+the+trauma+of+an+era%2Caps%2C110&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">a Mexican book on Edgar Allan Poe</a>.  I am learning a good deal from his new 700 pp. book <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Mexico-500-Year-History-Paul-Gillingham/dp/0802164846/ref=sr_1_1?crid=2GL12LV8NB6B8&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.utLhtnsVCdKxy6gR2_JjeWvFeSSBn7LTznCA537r8muMAU-aF3owldo3lCbMDJYL3T1SwSQGRnAcFv3v5lFwlnBgp4pcOt-EpK88bSbw933EJkgA-RCV5EVgl-gYLzn7icu8lp0uddxv32I4IUIcI_D_YouHQfhE5lwSqWKhnPAKAiGxuy6vM25A5Cc6APmHK4l8jh1sCJcHBHNk3EBEirPPcinm1wkzgYhBtmPNvxI.briugTxiM2o49ZDyErq8CmOIwrqpJq7U_R0-V1in4og&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=paul+gillingham&amp;qid=1770129411&amp;sprefix=paul+gillin%2Caps%2C108&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Mexico: A 500-Year History</a>, and I very much like his earlier work on Mexico and violence.  Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/11/19/books/review/mexico-paul-gillingham.html\" target=\"_blank\">an NYT review of the new book</a>.</p>\r\n<p>So what should I ask him?<